      <memberdef kind="function" id="struct_a_g_e_1_1_statistics_1a8817d663a8b2d6ecafb61e4e7b492bc7" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>uint32_t</type>
        <definition>uint32_t AGE::Statistics::GetTotalQuadIndexCount</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>GetTotalQuadIndexCount</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGE::Statistics::GetTotalQuadIndexCount</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function returns the total number of indices used by all quads in the scene. Each quad is composed of four vertices and each vertex has three coordinates, so a quad uses 24 indices. The function multiplies the number of quads (QuadCount) by 6 to get the total index count. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>uint32_t Total number of indices used by all quads in the scene.</para>
</simplesect>
This function returns the total number of indices used by all quads in the system. The count is calculated as the product of the quad count and 6, representing each quad&apos;s four triangles (2 triangles per face) and three vertices per triangle.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>uint32_t Total index count for all quads. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
