        <name>GetTotalPyramidIndexCount</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGE::Statistics::GetTotalPyramidIndexCount</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function calculates the total number of indices in a pyramid. The pyramid is represented as an array where each element represents a cube. Each cube has 6 faces, so to get the total number of indices, we multiply the number of cubes by 6. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>uint32_t Total number of indices in the pyramid.</para>
</simplesect>
This function calculates the total number of indices in a pyramid. The pyramid is represented as an equilateral triangle and each face of the triangle is a cube, so the total number of cubes that make up the pyramid is multiplied by 6 to get the total number of indices. <simplesect kind="return"><para>uint32_t This function returns the total number of indices in the pyramid as an unsigned 32-bit integer. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
